             New evaluation of chromium isotopes                  2437 1451
                 BNL, ORNL, IAEA - August 2020                    2437 1451
                                                                  2437 1451
       G.P.A. Nobre, M.T. Pigni, D.A. Brown, R. Capote, A. Trkov, 2437 1451
 K.H. Guber, R. Arcilla, J. Gutierrez, A. Cuadra, G. Arbanas      2437 1451
                                                                  2437 1451
Resolved Resonance Region:                                        2437 1451
                                                                  2437 1451
For 54Cr, RRR, defined up to the threshold of the first           2437 1451
inelastic, was taken from ENDF/B-VIII.0, including the DSD        2437 1451
capture background.                                               2437 1451
                                                                  2437 1451
Angular distributions were reconstructed from resonance           2437 1451
parameters using the Blatt-Biedenharn formalism and then were     2437 1451
minimally smoothed so that their energy dependence could be       2437 1451
represented as faithfully as possible given the limitations of    2437 1451
the ENDF format.                                                  2437 1451
                                                                  2437 1451
                                                                  2437 1451
Fast region:                                                      2437 1451
                                                                  2437 1451
Above the inelastic threshold, the nuclear reaction model         2437 1451
code EMPIRE-3.2.3 Malta (SVN rev.  5170; source rev.  5168) was   2437 1451
employed. Optical model calculations were performed using the     2437 1451
dispersive soft-rotor optical potential of Li et al. (RIPL #616)  2437 1451
through the OPTMAN module of EMPIRE.                              2437 1451
                                                                  2437 1451
Generally, fast-range model parameters were fitted to improve     2437 1451
agreement with partial inelastic data of Karatzas (up             2437 1451
to 3.12 MeV), and (n,p) and (n,a) cross-section data.             2437 1451
                                                                  2437 1451
                                                                  2437 1451
