***************************************************************** 2437 1451
 24-Cr- 54 ORNL Resonance Evaluation Including Covariance         2437 1451
                                                                  2437 1451
 L. C. Leal, H. Derrien, K. Guber, G. Arbanas and D. Wiarda       2437 1451
                                                                  2437 1451
   Resolved resonance parameter evaluation for Cr-54 was done with2437 1451
the computer code SAMMY. Transmission measurements for highly     2437 1451
enriched samples of chromium isotopes, done by Harvey et al., were2437 1451
used in the evaluations.[1] One transmission measurement for Cr-542437 1451
done with a 99.87% enriched sample were used in the evaluation.   2437 1451
The transmission measurement was done at the Oak Ridge Electron   2437 1451
Linear Accelerator (ORELA) of the Oak Ridge National Laboratory.  2437 1451
The transmission data were measured at the 201-meter flight-path  2437 1451
in the energy range of 13-850 KeV. Thermal cross section data     2437 1451
available in the EXFOR data system were also included in the      2437 1451
evaluation.                                                       2437 1451
                                                                  2437 1451
   A set of resonance parameter describing the experimental data  2437 1451
was obtained. Resonance parameter covariance matrices were also   2437 1451
obtained in the SAMMY evaluation process. The Cr-54 evaluation was2437 1451
done in the energy region 10-5 eV 834 keV.[2]                     2437 1451
  Thermal cross section obtained in the present evaluation are    2437 1451
compared to the values listed in the Atlas of Neutron Resoances   2437 1451
in the following table:                                           2437 1451
                                                                  2437 1451
    Cross Section            ORNL                      Atlas      2437 1451
                                                                  2437 1451
       Capt                0.41+/-0.04               0.41+/-0.04  2437 1451
       Total               2.96+/-0.11                   -        2437 1451
       Scat                2.55+/-0.10               2.54+/-0.10  2437 1451
                                                                  2437 1451
                    ORNL          ENDFBVII.0        JENDL4        2437 1451
      Res. Int  0.214+/-0.021       0.202            0.204        2437 1451
                                                         -        2437 1451
                                                                  2437 1451
 [ref 1] J. Harvey, personal communication, Transmission Data for 2437 1451
         Chromium Isotopes, January 2007.                         2437 1451
 [ref 2] Evaluation of the Chromium Resonance Parameters Including2437 1451
         Resonance Parameter Covariance, L. Leal, H. Derrien      2437 1451
         K. Guber, G. Arbanas, and D. Wiarda, International       2437 1451
         Conference on Nuclear Data for Science and Technology    2437 1451
         (ND2010), Jeju Island, Korea, April 26-30, 2010.         2437 1451
