                                                                  2437 1451
 ENDF/B-VI MOD 1 Evaluation, November 1989, D. Hetrick,           2437 1451
           D. Larson, N. Larson, and C. Fu (ORNL)                 2437 1451
                                                                  2437 1451
   This work employed the Hauser-Feshbach code TNG [Fu88,Fu80,    2437 1451
 Sh86]. The TNG code provides energy and angular distributions of 2437 1451
 particles emitted in the compound and pre-compound reactions,    2437 1451
 ensures consistency among all reactions, and maintains energy    2437 1451
 balance. Details pertinent to the contents of this evaluation    2437 1451
 will be published at a later date.                               2437 1451
                                                                  2437 1451
 Description of files ------------------------------------------- 2437 1451
 (MF-MT)                                                          2437 1451
  1-451 General information, references, and definitions.         2437 1451
  2-151 Resonance parameters;  used to provide the total,         2437 1451
        scattering, and capture cross sections from 1.E-5 eV to   2437 1451
        900 keV.  The resonance parameters are taken from Agrawal 2437 1451
        et al. [Ag84] and Allen and Musgrove [Al77], and          2437 1451
        readjusted to attempt to match the thermal values.  A     2437 1451
        background file in 3-1 is used from 11-900 keV.           2437 1451
        Note that the flag has been set to allow user calculation 2437 1451
        of the angular distributions from the R-Matrix resonance  2437 1451
        parameters, if the user wants angular distributions on    2437 1451
        a finer energy grid than given in 4-2.                    2437 1451
  3-1   Total cross section; given by resonance parameters up to  2437 1451
        900 keV with negative energy resonances adjusted to give  2437 1451
        measured thermal scattering and capture cross sections.   2437 1451
        Above 900 keV, isotopic data used to 4.0 MeV from Harvey  2437 1451
        and Agrawal [Ha88] and from 4.0-20.0 MeV high resolution  2437 1451
        natural Cr transmission measurements were used from       2437 1451
        Larson et al. [La88].                                     2437 1451
  3-2   Elastic scattering cross sections were obtained by        2437 1451
        subtracting the nonelastic from the total                 2437 1451
  3-3   Nonelastic cross section; sum of 3-4, 3-16, 3-102,        2437 1451
        3-103, and 3-107.                                         2437 1451
  3-4   Total inelastic cross section; sum of 3-51, 3-52, ...     2437 1451
        ...,3-54, and 3-91                                        2437 1451
  3-16  (n,2n) cross section; calculated by the TNG code.         2437 1451
        No data available.                                        2437 1451
  3-51 to 3-54 Inelastic scattering exciting levels; results are  2437 1451
        from TNG.                                                 2437 1451
  3-91  Inelastic scattering exciting the continuum; Calculated   2437 1451
        by TNG.                                                   2437 1451
  3-102 (n,g) capture cross section; given by resonance parameters2437 1451
        up to 900 keV; from 900 keV to 20 MeV, TNG calculations   2437 1451
        were used but normalized to measured average capture      2437 1451
        between 100 keV and 900 keV.  TNG calculations included a 2437 1451
        precompound component and weighted cross sections from    2437 1451
        all isotopes of Cr give 0.82 mb at 14.5 MeV, in agreement 2437 1451
        with the measurement of 0.75 mb for natural Cr.           2437 1451
  3-103 (n,p) cross section; calculated by the TNG code.          2437 1451
        Calculations agree well with data.                        2437 1451
  3-107 (n,a) cross section; calculated by the TNG code.          2437 1451
        Calculations agree well with data.                        2437 1451
  4-2   Angular distributions of secondary neutrons for elastic   2437 1451
        scattering; from ENDF/B-V.                                2437 1451
        If desired, angular distributions can be calculated by    2437 1451
        the user on a finer energy grid from the R-Matrix         2437 1451
        resonance parameters in 2-151.                            2437 1451
  6-16  (n,2n) reaction; includes simple constant yields for the  2437 1451
        neutron and 53Cr residual, and energy dependent yield     2437 1451
        based on TNG calculated gamma-ray spectra for the gamma   2437 1451
        ray; TNG calculated normalized distributions are given    2437 1451
        for each product.  Isotropy is assumed.                   2437 1451
  6-51 through 6-54 Inelastic scattering exciting levels;         2437 1451
        assumed isotropic.                                        2437 1451
  6-91  Inelastic scattering exciting the continuum; includes     2437 1451
        simple constant yields for the neutron and 54Cr residual  2437 1451
        and energy dependent yield based on TNG calculated gamma- 2437 1451
        ray spectra for the gamma ray; TNG calculated normalized  2437 1451
        distributions are given for each.  Isotropy is assumed.   2437 1451
  6-103 (n,p) reaction; includes simple constant yields for p     2437 1451
        and 54V residual, and energy dependent yield based on     2437 1451
        calculated gamma-ray spectra for gamma ray; calculated    2437 1451
        normalized distributions are given for each product.      2437 1451
        Isotropy is assumed.                                      2437 1451
  6-107 (n,a) reaction; includes simple constant yields for a     2437 1451
        and 51Ti residual, and energy dependent yield based on    2437 1451
        calculated gamma-ray spectra for gamma ray; calculated    2437 1451
        normalized distributions are given for each product.      2437 1451
        Isotropy is assumed.                                      2437 1451
 12-51 through 12-54 Branching ratios for the levels are given.   2437 1451
 12-102 (n,g) capture;  TNG calculated.                           2437 1451
 14-51 through 14-54 and 14-102 Gamma ray angular distributions   2437 1451
        assumed to be isotropic.                                  2437 1451
 15-102 (n,g) capture;  TNG calculated.                           2437 1451
                                                                  2437 1451
 ---------------------------------------------------------------- 2437 1451
 Uncertainty files                                                2437 1451
    An LB=8 section is included for all non-derived files as      2437 1451
        required by ENDF/B-VI.                                    2437 1451
                                                                  2437 1451
 33-1   Uncertainties are derived from 1.E-5 to 100 eV.  From 100 2437 1451
        eV to 20 MeV they are explicit, using LB=0,1 and 8.       2437 1451
 33-2   From 1.E-5 to 100 eV, uncertainties are explicit, based   2437 1451
        upon thermal uncertainty and other data.  From 100 eV to  2437 1451
        20 MeV the files are derived.                             2437 1451
 33-3   From 1.E-5 to 900 keV uncertainties are derived.  From    2437 1451
        900 keV to 20 MeV uncertainties are explicit, using LB=1  2437 1451
        and 8.                                                    2437 1451
 33-4   Uncertainties are all derived.                            2437 1451
 33-16  Uncertainties for (n,2n) are explicit, estimated from TNG.2437 1451
 33-51 through 3-91  Uncertainties for inelastic scattering are   2437 1451
        explicit, based on data and calculation uncertainties.    2437 1451
 33-102 Uncertainties are explicit, based on thermal data at low  2437 1451
        energies, and calculated results above 900 keV.           2437 1451
 33-103 Uncertainties estimated from TNG.                         2437 1451
 33-107 Uncertainties estimated from TNG.                         2437 1451
